 "new_string": "## Confirmed period-4 c-r variant (16×16 test)\nA separate instance had diagonal color tracks repeating horizontally as `[6,9,8,5]` and shifting one cell right in each successive row. The correct output was a full field with `output[r][c] = seq[(c-r) mod 4]`, `seq=[6,9,8,5]` (zero-indexed). Thus row 0 starts `[6,9,8,5,...]`, row 1 `[5,6,9,8,...]`, row 2 `[8,5,6,9,...]`, row 3 `[9,8,5,6,...]`, then repeats every 4 rows. The test's diagonal tracks validate it: 6 at (0,4),(1,5),…; 9 at (0,5),(1,6),…; 8 at (0,6),(1,7),…; 5 at (9,0),(10,1),…; these all preserve phase under c-r. A demo with horizontal stripes that replaced only row 0 background by 7 and retained repeated bands establishes this family can map 0 to an actual phase color and that the marker data encode a periodic color field. Correct submission confirmed.\n\n## Additional solved variant (current instance)\n"
